Licence inheritance for the benchmark runner binaries
======================================================

The benchmark consists of a Python orchestrator plus one runner binary per
baseline. Each binary inherits the licences of its statically linked
dependencies. Per-upstream details (URL, pinned SHA/tag, vendored scope) are
in third_party/<dep>/PROVENANCE.txt and, for the OnPair library, in
external/onpair_cpp.cmake.

Permissive-only binaries
------------------------
  uncompressed_runner   (no third-party deps)
  onpair_runner         OnPair library (MIT, via FetchContent pin)
  fsst_runner           FSST (MIT)
  lz4_runner            LZ4 lib/ subset (BSD-2-Clause)
  zstd_runner           Zstandard (BSD-3-Clause arm of the dual licence)
  rlz_runner            libdivsufsort (MIT); RLZ algorithm implemented
                        in-repo (runners/rlz/rlz_core.{h,cpp})
  bpe_runner            SentencePiece v0.2.2 (Apache-2.0) with its bundled
                        permissive snapshots and Abseil, which its build
                        fetches (abseil-cpp Apache-2.0, protobuf-lite
                        BSD-3-Clause-Google, darts_clone BSD-2-Clause,
                        esaxx MIT)

repair_runner — LGPL-2.1
------------------------
Statically links libCSD (LGPL-2.1, Martinez-Prieto et al.), including its
bundled libcds 1.0.x (LGPL-2.1). LGPL obligations are satisfied by full
source distribution of this repository: the complete library source and the
build system needed to relink are included under third_party/libcsd/.

Test-only dependencies (not linked into any measured binary)
------------------------------------------------------------
  minbpe (MIT) — secondary round-trip cross-check in the BPE tests.

